speechtext:
There is no particular advantage except that it is difficult to write to a man and call him "Dear member of the board". The title of "commissioner" is a little bit more distinctive, that is all. There is nothing more in it than that.
I can now give the names of the members of the advisory committee. I find this list in the annual report of the wheat board already tabled. The members of the advisory committee during the crop year 1951-52 were: L. Hutchinson, chairman, Calgary, Alberta;
D.	I. Walker, Toronto, Ontario; J. C. A. Nijdam, Winnipeg, Manitoba; F. H. Clenden-ning, Vancouver, British Columbia; J. Theo Roy, Montreal, Quebec; J. H. Wesson, Regina, Saskatchewan; R. C. Brown, Winnipeg, Manitoba; F. Pettypiece, Auld, Ontario; J. A. McCowan, Summerberry, Saskatchewan; P. Farnalls, Halkirk, Alberta; C. E. Hayles, Winnipeg, Manitoba. Of those-
